t. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.cor-mersenne-height"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.cor-mersenne-height"],"id":"long.cor-mersenne-height","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Corollary 10.14 (Mersenne specialisation)","locator":"Long record Corollary 10.14, p. 119, label cor:mersenne-height","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $x$ be a positive rational number and let $r\\ge0$, $n\\ge1$ be integers. If $2^r\\mid x.\\mathrm{num}.\\mathrm{natAbs}$ and $x<2/(2^n-1)$, then $2^r\\cdot(2^n-1) < 2\\cdot x.\\mathrm{den}$ ; a numerator $2$-power lower bound plus a Mersenne-scale upper bound on $x$ together force a denominator lower bound, *without* introducing a global prefix LCM. To see the inequality directly, write $x=a/b$ in lowest terms with $a,b>0$. The hypotheses give $a\\ge2^r$ and $a(2^n-1)<2b$. The conclusion follows by substitution. An application of Lemma 10.13 must in addition supply its denominator-divisibility assumptions.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.cor-mersenne-height","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.cor-mersenne-height","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.cor-mersenne-height%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mersenne_height%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.cor-mersenne-height%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mersenne_height%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_mersenne_height"},{"derived":true,"family"